\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces End-to-end DCGAI pipeline. Source document text is parsed by DMRST into an RST tree. Inference-bearing relations (CAUSE-RESULT, CONDITION, PURPOSE, CONTRAST/CONCESSION) are mapped to coarse axiom schemas. An LLM instantiates predicate content for each schema, guided by the nucleus and satellite EDU segments and the current KB predicate list (canonicalization). The resulting T2 axioms are added to the SWI-Prolog KB alongside T1 content predicates from sentence-level FOL extraction. SWI-Prolog runs backward chaining; proof failures are classified as content-miss vs.\ discourse-axiom-miss for targeted re-querying.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{End-to-end DCGAI pipeline. Source document text is parsed by DMRST into an RST tree. Inference-bearing relations (CAUSE-RESULT, CONDITION, PURPOSE, CONTRAST/CONCESSION) are mapped to coarse axiom schemas. An LLM instantiates predicate content for each schema, guided by the nucleus and satellite EDU segments and the current KB predicate list (canonicalization). The resulting T2 axioms are added to the SWI-Prolog KB alongside T1 content predicates from sentence-level FOL extraction. SWI-Prolog runs backward chaining; proof failures are classified as content-miss vs.\ discourse-axiom-miss for targeted re-querying}{figure.1}{}}
